<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18737" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraxĭnus</span></b> ,
		i, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an ash-tree</i>, <i>ash</i>,
			remarkable for its slenderness: Fraxinus excelsior, Linn.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				13, 24, § 62</span></i> et saep.; Enn. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 6, 2</span></i> (Ann. v. 195 ed.
			Vahl.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraxinus in silvis pulcherrima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 7, 65</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. G. 2, 359</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				25, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7, 677
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an ashen spear</i>
			or <i>javelin</i> (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraxinea hasta, v. the prec. art.),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 143</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">12, 122</span></i>; <i><span class="en">324</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 6,
				102</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
